 Administration is asking for public comment on an exemption application filed by Nick Castello. The request would let state licensing agencies issue non-domiciled commercial learner&#x27;s permits and CDLs to drivers in humanitarian or protection-based categories, including Uniting for Ukraine, Temporary Protected Status, asylum and pending asylum. The notice does not signal how the agency will decide; FMCSA will grant or deny the request after reviewing the application, safety analyses and comments.

The notice points to a final rule published February 13, 2026, which bars these permits and licenses unless the applicant shows lawful immigration status. The listed categories under that rule are H-2A, H-2B and E-2. Castello, described as a U.S. Marine Corps veteran and disabled veteran business owner, asks for relief of up to five years or a shorter period, and says he collected 93 responses from drivers reporting recurring problems with non-domiciled transactions. Comments are due December 24, 2026, under docket FMCSA-2026-3268.</description></item><item><title>Trucker Path app launches free CB radio feature</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/trucker-path-app-launches-free-cb-radio-feature-a2b6ef683e/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/trucker-path-app-launches-free-cb-radio-feature-a2b6ef683e/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 04:26:27 +0000</pubDate><category>Equipment</category><description>Commercial Carrier Journal</description></item><item><title>Diesel prices soar as Silicon Valley startup unveils cab-less trucking solution</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/diesel-prices-soar-as-silicon-valley-startup-unveils-cab-less-trucking-5c25dc2917/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/diesel-prices-soar-as-silicon-valley-startup-unveils-cab-less-trucking-5c25dc2917/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:27:06 +0000</pubDate><category>Fuel</category><description>Fox Business</description></item><item><title>CRST Drivers Win $1.8M In Truck Lease Case</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/crst-drivers-win-1-8m-in-truck-lease-case-dcc5f006b3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/crst-drivers-win-1-8m-in-truck-lease-case-dcc5f006b3/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:26:14 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>An Iowa federal judge awarded nearly $1.8 million to close to 1,000 drivers that CRST underpaid under their leases, rejecting the company&#x27;s bid to deny recovery o