aultimes.com/story/upcoming-mark-colson-s-vision-for-ata-and-trucking-s-future-78fd83d3a8/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:15:07 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Mark Colson has started as president and CEO of American Trucking Associations. In a TT Newsmakers video with Seth Clevenger, he is set to discuss his background, his leadership approach and his priorities for his first year at ATA. The conversation will also cover how ATA can strengthen links between national and state associations and build bipartisan backing in Washington. Viewers can return to the Transport Topics page on December 7 to watch the full discussion.</description></item><item><title>Colorado Approves Chain-Up Assistance Program for Truckers</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/colorado-approves-chain-up-assistance-program-for-truckers-fc2f8d80fb/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/colorado-approves-chain-up-assistance-program-for-truckers-fc2f8d80fb/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:14:03 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Wisevoter</description></item><item><title>One by one, non-domiciled CDL holders seek exemption</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/one-by-one-non-domiciled-cdl-holders-seek-exemption-2e343b6e1c/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/one-by-one-non-domiciled-cdl-holders-seek-exemption-2e343b6e1c/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:26:49 +0000</pubDate><category>Regulations</category><description>Land Line Media</description></item><item><title>Freight Fraud and Cargo Theft Shift Ahead of 2026 Peak Season</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/freight-fraud-and-cargo-theft-shift-ahead-of-2026-peak-season-f219319f35/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/freight-fraud-and-cargo-theft-shift-ahead-of-2026-peak-season-f219319f35/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:20:55 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Commercial Carrier Journal</description></item><item><title>Port truckers face cargo hurdles as imports hit record</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/port-truckers-face-cargo-hurdles-as-imports-hit-record-576658f9e4/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/port-truckers-face-cargo-hurdles-as-imports-hit-record-576658f9e4/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:00:00 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Transport Topics</description></item><item><title>Trucking industry rallies behind SCF to celebrate 20 years of helping truckers</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/trucking-industry-rallies-behind-scf-to-celebrate-20-years-of-helping-f8953c6c2b/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/trucking-industry-rallies-behind-scf-to-celebrate-20-years-of-helping-f8953c6c2b/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:41:37 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>The St. Christopher Truckers Relief Fund (SCF) said it has secured more than $800,000 in gifts and pledges for 2026 from trucking companies, associations and industry partners. Contributors named in the announcement include Love&#x27;s Travel Stops, TravelCenters of America, OOIDA and Total Quality Logistics. Since it began, the nonprofit said it has assisted nearly 4,200 professional drivers and provided over $5.5 million in direct financial aid. SCF plans a yearlong 20th anniversary effort in 2027 and will mark the milestone at the Mid-America Trucking Show in March. The organization also runs health programs covering diabetes prevention, cancer screenings and tobacco cessation for over-the-road drivers.</description></item><item><title>Vintage Modern Expands Beyond Modern Classic Trucks With Handcrafted Fastback</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/vintage-modern-expands-beyond-modern-classic-trucks-with-handcrafted-f-182ae7741c/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/vintage-modern-expands-beyond-modern-classic-trucks-with-handcrafted-f-182ae7741c/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:40:15 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>THE SHOP</description></item><item><title>Bank challenges trucking CEO’s $8.5M Florida estate amid bankruptcy</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/bank-challenges-trucking-ceo-s-8-5m-florida-estate-amid-bankruptcy-baad5f3dc7/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/bank-challenges-trucking-ceo-s-8-5m-florida-estate-amid-bankruptcy-baad5f3dc7/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:16:37 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Child killed in crash involving SUV, semi-truck on Regina Bypass</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/child-killed-in-crash-involving-suv-semi-truck-on-regina-bypass-6d6c3a6cad/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/child-killed-in-crash-involving-suv-semi-truck-on-regina-bypass-6d6c3a6cad/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:04:40 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Global News</description></item><item><title>Oregon sheriff says several truck drivers admitted to skipping the weigh station after seeing &#x27;open&#x27; sign</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/oregon-sheriff-says-several-truck-drivers-admitted-to-skipping-the-wei-464a4eec54/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/oregon-sheriff-says-several-truck-drivers-admitted-to-skipping-the-wei-464a4eec54/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 17:39:05 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>The Clackamas County Sheriff&#x27;s Office said it took part in a weigh station enforcement operation that led to citations for dozens of truck drivers. The six-hour operation took place on October 28 at the Woodburn northbound and southbound weigh stations, where officers stopped 84 trucks that bypassed the open scale, according to the office&#x27;s November 22 update. The sheriff&#x27;s office said several drivers admitted they saw the scale was open and skipped it anyway. The Woodburn operation was one of three multi-agency trucking compliance details that the Oregon Department of Transportation released results for the week before, covering October and November 2026.</description></item><item><title>Small trucking firms scramble to survive diesel costs</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/small-trucking-firms-scramble-to-survive-diesel-costs-be8e1e697a/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/small-trucking-firms-scramble-to-survive-diesel-costs-be8e1e697a/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 17:35:57 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Transport Topics</description></item><item><title>Lufthansa Cargo to buy out 2nd ground agent at Frankfurt airport</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/lufthansa-cargo-to-buy-out-2nd-ground-agent-at-frankfurt-airport-d02f76afc7/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/lufthansa-cargo-to-buy-out-2nd-ground-agent-at-frankfurt-airport-d02f76afc7/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 17:32:21 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>FreightWaves</description></item><item><title>Lubrication choices can drive down fleet costs</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/lubrication-choices-can-drive-down-fleet-costs-5f125efbdc/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/lubrication-choices-can-drive-down-fleet-costs-5f125efbdc/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 17:02:59 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>Truck News</description></item><item><title>WEX Fleet One - Fuel Payments for Truckers</title><link>https://haultimes.com/story/wex-fleet-one-fuel-payments-for-truckers-45b25d6ef5/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://haultimes.com/story/wex-fleet-one-fuel-payments-for-truckers-45b25d6ef5/</guid><pubDate>Mon, 23 Nov 2026 17:01:50 +0000</pubDate><category>Industry</category><description>yespress.io</description></item><item><title>AI Should Make Dispatchers Better, N